@startuml state-digitalizer-book
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: a book's status is driven only by its runs and by operator decisions;
'       a FULL run renders and then gates, so the reviewer sees the PDF; a
'       passing gate approves it, and only an approved book is published
'       (re-runs reopen it).
' Kind: UML state machine, one Book, proposal. The run and job machines that
'       drive these transitions are in state-digitalizer-run-job.
' Source: this repo docs/design/studio-spec.md (statuses discovered/queued/
'         running/review/approved/published/error, studio.gate, ordering of
'         RENDER then PUBLISH runs), studio/workers/stages/orchestrate.py (STAGES:
'         FULL = clean, analyze, formulas, render, gate) and gate.py (approved /
'         review, publish run when auto_publish = "gate") (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Book lifecycle in the portal (proposal, 2026-11-16)

[*] --> discovered : import (scan tree listed)

state discovered
state queued : a FULL run is waiting
state running : FULL run: clean, analyze,\nrender, gate (or a RERUN)
state review <<focus>> : gate flagged it;\noperator edits pages,\nregions, metadata
state approved : outputs final (PDF, PDF/A,\nEPUB, IA item); PUBLISH\nqueued only with a catalog target
state published : optional: entry +\nacquisitions in the catalog
state error : last run failed\n(error kept on the run)

discovered --> queued : operator or batch\nstarts a run
queued --> running : orchestrator dispatches\nthe first job
running --> review : gate: flags or\nlow score
running --> approved : gate passed
review --> running : page re-run\n(interactive)
review --> approved : operator approves
approved --> published : publish run done\n(optional)
approved --> running : re-run
published --> running : re-run after\npublication
running --> error : run failed
approved --> error : render or\npublish failed
error --> queued : retry

caption Status is a projection of runs plus operator decisions, never set by a worker. Approved is a valid end state:\npublication is optional. A re-run goes through the gate again; a published book republishes (upload, then delete old files).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/state-digitalizer-book.puml
@enduml
